#
# The injection is surgical rather than a revert of the commit: it restores the
# 724973d predicate verbatim over the catalog-derived index alone —
# `matching.len() > 1 || any(link.claim != claim)`, with `matching.len() > 1`
# retained — and deletes nothing else. `enumerate_recovery_origin_links` stays
# in the file and goes dead, which is why the red run also carries a `dead_code`
# warning; that warning is incidental and is not part of the signature.
exit: 101

# ===== THE RESOLVER PICKED AN AUTHORITY IT COULD NOT SEE ALL OF =============
#
# TWO failures, and they are the same defect at two widths.
#
# Width 1 — a SILENT index. Both replacements are live and appending, so both
# catalog records are invalidated and the production collector reports nothing.
# The injected predicate reads that emptiness as "nothing contradicts the claim
# I loaded" and returns `Valid`.
contains: a second authenticated replacement hidden by an invalidated catalog record must still fail closed, got Valid(

# Width 2 — a PARTIALLY LOADED index, and the likelier arrangement of the two
# because it needs one live appender rather than two. The collector holds
# exactly one link, that link IS the loaded claim's, and the index therefore
# reads as unanimous confirmation. It is not: the second authenticated
# replacement's record is simply not loaded. `matching.len() > 1` is false, so
# the injected predicate finds nothing contradictory and returns `Valid` here
# too. This is the case a fix that enumerated only on a zero match would miss.
contains: an index holding one link and blind to a second authenticated replacement must not confirm uniqueness, got Valid(

# `Valid(` in both panics is the admission itself — `/api/runs/<id>/recover`
# answers with exactly this claim and inventory then clears the run's recovery
# actions. Both claims are for THIS origin, so this is authority selection and
# not some unrelated claim leaking through. The replacement run ids are minted
# with a timestamp and are deliberately not pinned.
contains: origin_run_id: "run-hidden-origin"

# ===== AND NOTHING ELSE MOVED ==============================================
#
# EXACTLY TWO failures out of twenty. The eighteen that stay green include both
# tests that would otherwise make this look like a wholesale break rather than a
# width dispute:
